export default "<p class=\"article-lead\">AI is moving faster than any technology in business history. Most leaders know it matters. Very few know what to do about it. That changes today.</p>\n\n        <p>Good morning. Welcome to the very first edition of SundAI Motivation.</p>\n\n        <p>My name is Remco Vroom. I'm Global EVP of MarTech AI Transformation at Monks, and I've spent the last 30 years at the intersection of marketing, technology, and business transformation. In that time, I've watched every major technology wave arrive, and I've watched the same pattern repeat every single time: the leaders who understood first, won first.</p>\n\n        <p>AI is different. Not because it's more hyped, every wave has hype, but because it moves faster than anything we've ever seen. In 2020, the world saw <strong>11 notable AI models</strong>. In 2024, that number was <strong>81</strong>. In 2025, we stopped counting because meaningful releases happen weekly. The acceleration isn't slowing. It's compounding.</p>\n\n        <p>And here's the problem. If AI isn't your full-time job, you've already fallen behind on what it can do. Not six months behind. Weeks behind. The gap between what AI is capable of right now and what most business leaders believe it's capable of is the single biggest strategic blind spot in the market.</p>\n\n        <hr>\n\n        <h3>Why I Started This</h3>\n\n        <p>I kept having the same conversation. In boardrooms. At dinners. On flights. Smart, accomplished leaders, CEOs, CMOs, CFOs, pulling me aside to ask the same question: \"Remco, what should I actually be doing about AI?\"</p>\n\n        <p>Not the hype version. Not the vendor pitch. The real version. What does AI mean for my business, my team, my decisions, this quarter?</p>\n\n        <p>That question deserves a real answer. Not a 90-page whitepaper. Not a webinar. Not a LinkedIn post full of buzzwords. A clear, honest, weekly briefing that respects your time and your intelligence.</p>\n\n        <p>That's what SundAI Motivation is.</p>\n\n        <hr>\n\n        <h3>What You'll Get Every Sunday</h3>\n\n        <p>Every week, this series delivers one focused article. Each one follows a simple structure:</p>\n\n        <ul>\n          <li><strong>The headline</strong>: What's happening in AI right now that you need to know about</li>\n          <li><strong>The context</strong>: Why it matters for your business, explained without jargon</li>\n          <li><strong>The real example</strong>: How companies are actually dealing with this, what works and what doesn't</li>\n          <li><strong>Your one action</strong>: One specific thing you can do this week to move your organization forward</li>\n        </ul>\n\n        <p>No fluff. No filler. No \"AI will change everything\" without telling you how. Just signal.</p>\n\n        <hr>\n\n        <h3>Who This Is For</h3>\n\n        <p>If you're a business leader, executive, or decision-maker who knows AI matters but doesn't have 20 hours a week to track it, this is for you. If you're tired of feeling like you need a computer science degree to understand what your team is proposing, this is for you. If you want to make better decisions about AI without becoming a technologist, this is for you.</p>\n\n        <p>You don't need to become an AI expert. You need to become an AI-literate leader. There's a massive difference, and that difference is exactly what this series is designed to build.</p>\n\n        <hr>\n\n        <h3>The 12-Week Journey Ahead</h3>\n\n        <p>Over the next 12 weeks, we're going to cover the full landscape of AI for business leaders:</p>\n\n        <h4>Weeks 1-4: Understanding the Terrain</h4>\n\n        <p>We start with what's actually happening, the real pace of change, the gap between ambition and execution, shadow AI in your workforce, and why so many CEOs are quietly terrified.</p>\n\n        <h4>Weeks 5-8: Building the Foundation</h4>\n\n        <p>Then we move to action, who's getting it right, why team resistance is your biggest threat, your first practical steps, and how to start without a massive budget.</p>\n\n        <h4>Weeks 9-12: Scaling with Confidence</h4>\n\n        <p>Finally, we go from pilot to impact, proving ROI to your board, the leadership model AI demands, bringing your whole company along, and why right now is the best time to start.</p>\n\n        <p>By the end, you won't just understand AI better. You'll have a framework for making decisions about it. That's the goal.</p>\n\n        <hr>\n\n        <div class=\"monks-story\">\n          <span class=\"monks-story-label\">A Note on Monks</span>\n          <p>I should be transparent about something. I lead AI transformation at <strong>Monks</strong>, one of the largest digital-first companies in the world, 6,500 people across 33 countries. We were named <strong>AI Agency of the Year</strong> by Adweek and <strong>AI Pioneer</strong> by The One Show. We built <strong>Monks.Flow</strong>, an AI-native marketing platform that's reshaping how the world's biggest brands create and deploy content.</p>\n          <p>I'll reference Monks throughout this series because I've seen firsthand what works at scale. But this series isn't a Monks sales pitch. It's a leadership resource. The insights apply whether you work with us or not. My goal is to help you think more clearly about AI, period.</p>\n        </div>\n\n        <blockquote>\n          <p>\"The gap between what AI can do and what most leaders think it can do is the biggest strategic blind spot in business today. This series exists to close that gap.\"</p>\n        </blockquote>\n\n        <hr>\n\n        <div class=\"action-callout\">\n          <div class=\"action-callout-label\">\n            <svg width=\"18\" height=\"18\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><path d=\"M13 2L3 14h9l-1 8 10-12h-9l1-8z\"/></svg>\n            Your First Action\n          </div>\n          <p>Here's what I'd like you to do this week, before the first full article drops next Sunday.</p>\n          <p><strong>Write down the three questions about AI that keep you up at night.</strong> Not the polished boardroom questions. The real ones. The ones you're embarrassed to ask because you feel like you should already know the answer.</p>\n          <p>Save them somewhere. Over the next 12 weeks, we're going to answer every single one of them. And if your question isn't covered, send it to me. I read everything.</p>\n          <p><strong>Welcome to SundAI Motivation. Let's make AI make sense.</strong></p>\n        </div>";
